# Pairs with RoutingConverges. An undo before the flip lifts the fence an
# interrupted swap left only on the pinned shard, not on the shard an adaptive
# split allocated above the pinned count (the issue-3880 shape), so k2's shard
# of T stays in Rejecting under an alias that still names T, and the tree's own
# pair is refused for k2 forever. Fairness is unchanged; no other operation is
# blocked, so the mutant cannot deadlock instead.
MODULE: RoutingConvergesUndoBeforeFlipKeepsFence
TARGET: RoutingConverges
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: an undo before the flip leaves the split-allocated shard fenced, so it refuses forever
PERTURBS: UndoBeforeFlip

--- FIND
    /\ rz \in {"snap", "copied"}
    /\ fence' = {}
    /\ rz' = "undone"
--- REPLACE
    /\ rz \in {"snap", "copied"}
\* MUTATION: only the pinned shard's fence is lifted.
    /\ fence' = fence \ {s1}
    /\ rz' = "undone"
--- END